# Calcinate — Stage 1 of the Magnum Opus

## Hard rules

1. No deletion without three-layer intent (Business + Architectural + Stylistic)
2. Reversible by construction (git per item)
3. Verify after every step (tests + build)
4. No batch removal
5. Agent surfaces, user approves

## What gets burned (four scans)

1. Code rot — unreferenced, dead branches, stale TODOs
2. Structural — unmaterialized abstractions, dumping grounds
3. Dependency — single-use packages, overlapping libs
4. Docs + tests — docs for nonexistent features, tests of framework

## Procedure

1. Declare three-layer intent
2. Dispatch four parallel scans
3. Produce tiered plan
4. Execute item by item with verify
5. Final report

## Anti-patterns

- Calcinate without intent
- Batch removal
- During feature work
- Aesthetically (not against intent)
- Without coagulate companion
